{title: Liberty to the Sword}
{subtitle: Jeremiah 34:8–22}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Em] | [Em] | [D] | [Am] |
| [Em] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The word came to Jeremiah from the Lord
After [C]Zedekiah made a covenant in the [G]land
To pro[C]claim liberty for all the people [Em]found
Set [Am]free your Hebrew [D]slaves so none held [Em]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
All the officials and the [G]people obeyed
[D]They set the male and female [Em]slaves at bay
[C]But afterward they changed their [G]minds and turned
[D]Took back the freed and forced [B]the laboring burned
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So now [Em]I proclaim liberty for [G]you
Lib[D]erty to the sword plague and famine [Em]too
I will [C]make you a horror to the [G]earth
Because you [D]broke the covenant in your [Em]birth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I made a covenant with your [G]fathers of old
[D]When I brought them out from the [Em]house of toil
[C]At the end of seven years [G]let them go free
[D]But they did not listen to what [B]I said to be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So [Em]now I proclaim liberty for [G]you
Lib[D]erty to the sword plague and famine [Em]too
I will [C]make you a horror to the [G]earth
Because you [D]broke the covenant in your [Em]birth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Like the calf they cut in two [G]and walked through
The [D]priests and the leaders broke the law and [Em]broke the vow
[C]Their corpses will be food for [G]birds in the sky
[D]And the beasts of the earth [B]under the eye
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will [Em]bring them back to this city of [G]stone
To [D]fight and to capture and to [Em]burn their home
{end_of_verse}

